{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory was otherwise strong: the doctor escalated to same-day emergency/psychiatric assessment, stopped family-directed sertraline/lorazepam use, secured medicines/dangerous items, and obtained a concrete hospital observation plan. However, RC1 was not fully met because the authored red-flag set included severe abdominal pain/distension, and the doctor’s safety-net lists omitted that domain. RC5 also remained imperfect because the doctor handled blurred documents safely but did not explicitly explain that a normal cranial CT does not rule out drug toxicity or psychiatric danger. These are minor responsibility-chain omissions, so the deterministic cap is grade 2 despite completed high-order work.",
